 focuses on the development and commercialization of transformative treatments for patients with immunological diseases. The company offers atacicept, a fully humanized TACI-Fc fusion protein that binds B-cell activating factor (BAFF) and A proliferation-inducing ligand (APRIL), which is self-administered at home as a subcutaneous injection being evaluated for the treatment of immunoglobulin A nephropathy (IgAN) and other autoimmune kidney diseases. It is also developing MAU868, a human monoclonal antibody for the treatment of BK viremia infections that has completed phase 2 clinical trial; and VT-109, a novel BAFF/APRIL dual-inhibitor B cell maturation antigen (BCMA) molecule to treat B cell mediated autoimmune diseases. The company was formerly known as Trucode Gene Repair, Inc. and changed its name to Vera Therapeutics, Inc. in April 2020. Vera Therapeutics, Inc. was incorporated in 2016 and is headquartered in Brisbane, California.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Marshall W. Fordyce M.D. | Founder, President, CEO & Director | Age 50 | Compensation: $1.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 249 people. Stock-based compensation of $152K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Vera Therapeutics, Inc. is a mid-cap healthcare business with a $2.1B market cap.","The company is burning through $242M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -41.9\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 1/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (21.5% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting ag